From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] diffraction: sample the full k-space in
 StaticStructureFactorDirect

tests/test_diffraction_static_structure_factor.py::TestStaticStructureFactorDirect::test_k_min
and ::test_random_system_2D fail deterministically (seed=1) across every
sf_params parametrization: many S(k) bins come back as exact 0.0 where a
differently-binned reference computation of the same system is clearly
nonzero, and high-k bins of a random 2D system average to ~0.42 instead of
the expected ~1. This reproduces identically from source inspection and is
not an artifact of this port's toolchain, TBB, or riscv64's int/float
conversion behaviour: StaticStructureFactorDirect::reciprocal_isotropic()
looped its grid indices as unsigned ints starting at 0 (`for (unsigned int
kx = begin; kx < end; ++kx)`, same for ky/kz), so it only ever sampled the
single positive octant (quadrant in 2D) of reciprocal space instead of an
isotropic sampling of the full sphere/circle. S(k) = S(-k) makes a half
space/half plane sufficient, but a single octant/quadrant is not: it biases
which k-vectors land in a given radial bin (explaining the exact-zero bins
test_k_min catches) and systematically undercounts the high-k shell average
test_random_system_2D checks. The pruning-distance formulas in
get_prune_distance2D/3D() were also normalized against that same
quadrant/octant area/volume, so num_sampled_k_points no longer means what it
says once the sampled region is widened.

This is already fixed upstream, on glotzerlab/freud's main branch, in two
commits not yet in any tagged release:

- 981697aad8014ef80393d29c1942b925406e7d7c "Sample all k vector directions
  in StaticStructureFactorDirect" switches the kx/ky/kz loops to signed
  indices over a half space (half plane in 2D), fixes the ky/kz range
  quadratic for triclinic boxes, and rescales the pruning constants to
  match the wider sampled region. It also adds
  test_oriented_system_against_full_grid, a new regression test that
  compares against a brute-force grid sum, and retunes two of the existing
  _sf_params() num_sampled_k_points values (2e3->8e3, 1e4->4e4) for the new
  pruning constants.
  https://github.com/glotzerlab/freud/commit/981697aad8014ef80393d29c1942b925406e7d7c

- 67b5dbf9907a7e7db37a0675439a58df7034c8bc "Implement changes suggested by
  DomFijan to be consistent with freud's convention and improve
  performance" is a small follow-up cleanup of the same function (size_t
  for the unsigned grid-size counters, and skipping the k_min hole by
  jumping the loop variable instead of `continue`).
  https://github.com/glotzerlab/freud/commit/67b5dbf9907a7e7db37a0675439a58df7034c8bc

This backports the net effect of both onto our pinned v3.6.1 tag, verified
to apply cleanly on top of it. A third, unrelated commit on main
(2daf773572f797050068d130b9bddca3cdbe0051) deletes test_against_dynasor
from the same test file in between these two; that test is already a no-op
in our CIBW_TEST_REQUIRES (dynasor is not installed, so
pytest.importorskip skips it) and is left alone here to keep this patch
scoped to the actual bug.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/glotzerlab/freud/commit/981697aad8014ef80393d29c1942b925406e7d7c]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 freud/diffraction/StaticStructureFactorDirect.cc  | 104 +++++++++++++----------
 tests/test_diffraction_static_structure_factor.py |  29 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

diff --git a/freud/diffraction/StaticStructureFactorDirect.cc b/freud/diffraction/StaticStructureFactorDirect.cc
index 0469520..6d946df 100644
--- a/freud/diffraction/StaticStructureFactorDirect.cc
+++ b/freud/diffraction/StaticStructureFactorDirect.cc
@@ -196,14 +196,16 @@ inline Eigen::Matrix2f box_to_matrix2D(const box::Box& box)

 inline float get_prune_distance3D(unsigned int num_sampled_k_points, float q_max, float q_volume)
 {
-    if ((num_sampled_k_points > M_PI * std::pow(q_max, 3.0) / (6 * q_volume)) || (num_sampled_k_points == 0))
+    if ((num_sampled_k_points > 2 * M_PI * std::pow(q_max, 3.0) / (3 * q_volume))
+        || (num_sampled_k_points == 0))
     {
         // Above this limit, all points are used and no pruning occurs.
         return std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
     }
     // We use Cardano's formula to compute the pruning distance.
     const auto p = -0.75F * q_max * q_max;
-    const auto q = 3.0F * static_cast<float>(num_sampled_k_points) * q_volume / static_cast<float>(M_PI)
+    const auto q
+        = 3.0F * static_cast<float>(num_sampled_k_points) * q_volume / (4.0F * static_cast<float>(M_PI))
         - q_max * q_max * q_max / 4.0F;
     const auto D = p * p * p / 27.0F + q * q / 4.0F;

@@ -215,7 +217,7 @@ inline float get_prune_distance3D(unsigned int num_sampled_k_points, float q_max

 inline float get_prune_distance2D(unsigned int num_sampled_k_points, float q_max, float q_area)
 {
-    if ((num_sampled_k_points > M_PI * std::pow(q_max, 2.0) / (4 * q_area)) || (num_sampled_k_points == 0))
+    if ((num_sampled_k_points > M_PI * std::pow(q_max, 2.0) / (2 * q_area)) || (num_sampled_k_points == 0))
     {
         // Above this limit, all points are used and no pruning occurs.
         return std::numeric_limits<float>::infinity();
@@ -223,11 +225,11 @@ inline float get_prune_distance2D(unsigned int num_sampled_k_points, float q_max

     // In 2D, a uniform radial sampling density is achieved when
     // p_keep(q) = min(1, q_prune / q). Solving the expected-point equation
-    // over the sampled quadrant gives:
-    // N = pi / (4 q_area) * (2 q_max q_prune - q_prune^2)
-    // => q_prune = q_max - sqrt(q_max^2 - 4 N q_area / pi).
+    // over the sampled half plane gives:
+    // N = pi / (2 q_area) * (2 q_max q_prune - q_prune^2)
+    // => q_prune = q_max - sqrt(q_max^2 - 2 N q_area / pi).
     const auto N = static_cast<float>(num_sampled_k_points);
-    const auto discriminant = std::max(0.0F, q_max * q_max - 4.0F * N * q_area / static_cast<float>(M_PI));
+    const auto discriminant = std::max(0.0F, q_max * q_max - 2.0F * N * q_area / static_cast<float>(M_PI));
     return q_max - std::sqrt(discriminant);
 }

@@ -239,16 +241,19 @@ std::mt19937 setup_rng(unsigned int seed)
     return std::mt19937(seed_seq);
 }

-// Function to evaluate quadratic equation for kz
-std::pair<unsigned int, unsigned int>
-evaluate_quadratic_equation(float coef_a, float coef_b, float coef_c_min, float coef_c_max, unsigned int N_kz)
+// Function to evaluate the integer range [lower, upper] bracketing the roots of a quadratic equation.
+// The range is empty (lower > upper) if there are no real roots.
+std::pair<int, int> evaluate_quadratic_equation(float coef_a, float coef_b, float coef_c)
 {
-    const auto b_over_2a = coef_b / (2 * coef_a);
-    const auto kz_min = static_cast<unsigned int>(
-        std::floor(-b_over_2a + std::sqrt(b_over_2a * b_over_2a - coef_c_min / coef_a)));
-    const auto kz_max = static_cast<unsigned int>(
-        std::ceil(-b_over_2a + std::sqrt(b_over_2a * b_over_2a - coef_c_max / coef_a)));
-    return {kz_min, std::min(kz_max, N_kz)};
+    const auto center = -coef_b / (2 * coef_a);
+    const auto discriminant = center * center - coef_c / coef_a;
+    if (discriminant < 0)
+    {
+        return {0, -1};
+    }
+    const auto half_width = std::sqrt(discriminant);
+    return {static_cast<int>(std::floor(center - half_width)),
+            static_cast<int>(std::ceil(center + half_width))};
 }

 // Function to evaluate if k_vector should be kept for 2D sampling.
@@ -299,41 +304,47 @@ std::vector<vec3<float>> StaticStructureFactorDirect::reciprocal_isotropic(const
         // Above the pruning distance, the grid of k points is sampled isotropically
         // at a lower density.
         const auto q_prune_distance = get_prune_distance2D(num_sampled_k_points, q_max, q_area);
-        const auto N_kx = static_cast<unsigned int>(std::ceil(q_max / dq_x));
-        const auto N_ky = static_cast<unsigned int>(std::ceil(q_max / dq_y));
+        const auto N_kx = static_cast<size_t>(std::ceil(q_max * box_matrix.row(0).norm()));
         const auto bx = freud::constants::TWO_PI * vec3<float>(B(0, 0), B(0, 1), 0.0);
         const auto by = freud::constants::TWO_PI * vec3<float>(B(1, 0), B(1, 1), 0.0);
+        // Since S(k) = S(-k), we only sample the half plane kx > 0 or (kx = 0 and ky >= 0).
         // This is a 2D loop but we parallelize in 1D because we only need to seed
         // the random number generators once per block and there is no benefit of
         // locality if we parallelize in 2D.
-        util::forLoopWrapper(0, N_kx, [&](size_t begin, size_t end) {
+        util::forLoopWrapper(0, N_kx + 1, [&](size_t begin, size_t end) {
             // Set up thread-local random number generator for k point
             // pruning.
             std::mt19937 rng = setup_rng(static_cast<unsigned int>(begin));
             std::uniform_real_distribution<float> base_dist(0, 1);
             const auto add_all_k_points = std::isinf(q_prune_distance);
-            for (unsigned int kx = begin; kx < end; ++kx)
+            for (size_t kx = begin; kx < end; ++kx)
             {
                 const auto k_vec_x = static_cast<float>(kx) * bx;

-                // Solve the quadratic equation for kz to limit which kz values we must sample:
-                // k_min^2 <= |k_vec_x|^2 + ky^2 |by|^2 - 2 ky (k_vec_x \cdot by) <= k_max^2
-                // 0 <= ky^2 (|by|^2) + ky (-2 (k_vec_x \cdot by)) + (|k_vec_x|^2 - k_min^2)
-                // 0 >= ky^2 (|by|^2) + ky (-2 (k_vec_x \cdot by)) + (|k_vec_x|^2 - k_max^2)
+                // Solve the quadratic equation for ky to limit which ky values we must sample:
+                // k_min^2 <= |k_vec_x|^2 + ky^2 |by|^2 + 2 ky (k_vec_x \cdot by) <= k_max^2
+                // 0 <= ky^2 (|by|^2) + ky (2 (k_vec_x \cdot by)) + (|k_vec_x|^2 - k_min^2)
+                // 0 >= ky^2 (|by|^2) + ky (2 (k_vec_x \cdot by)) + (|k_vec_x|^2 - k_max^2)
                 // This step improves performance significantly when k_min > 0
                 // by eliminating a large portion of the search space. Likewise,
                 // it eliminates the portion of search space outside a sphere
-                // with radius k_max. We round ky_min down and ky_max up to
+                // with radius k_max. We round the ranges outward to
                 // ensure that we don't accidentally throw out valid k points in
                 // the range (k_min, k_max) due to rounding error.
                 const auto coef_a = dot(by, by);
-                const auto coef_b = -2 * dot(k_vec_x, by);
+                const auto coef_b = 2 * dot(k_vec_x, by);
                 const auto coef_c_min = dot(k_vec_x, k_vec_x) - k_min * k_min;
                 const auto coef_c_max = dot(k_vec_x, k_vec_x) - k_max * k_max;
-                auto [ky_min, ky_max]
-                    = evaluate_quadratic_equation(coef_a, coef_b, coef_c_min, coef_c_max, N_ky);
-                for (unsigned int ky = ky_min; ky < std::min(ky_max, N_ky); ++ky)
+                const auto [ky_min, ky_max] = evaluate_quadratic_equation(coef_a, coef_b, coef_c_max);
+                const auto [ky_inner_min, ky_inner_max]
+                    = evaluate_quadratic_equation(coef_a, coef_b, coef_c_min);
+                for (int ky = (kx == 0) ? std::max(ky_min, 0) : ky_min; ky <= ky_max; ++ky)
                 {
+                    if (ky > ky_inner_min + 1 && ky < ky_inner_max - 1)
+                    {
+                        // Skip the k_min hole: jump to the first index past it.
+                        ky = ky_inner_max - 1;
+                    }
                     const auto k_vec = k_vec_x + static_cast<float>(ky) * by;
                     const auto q_distance_sq
                         = dot(k_vec, k_vec) / freud::constants::TWO_PI / freud::constants::TWO_PI;
@@ -366,43 +377,50 @@ std::vector<vec3<float>> StaticStructureFactorDirect::reciprocal_isotropic(const
         const auto bx = freud::constants::TWO_PI * vec3<float>(B(0, 0), B(0, 1), B(0, 2));
         const auto by = freud::constants::TWO_PI * vec3<float>(B(1, 0), B(1, 1), B(1, 2));
